 {'idx': 18, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'be seen from some places, like "Horben". Lindenberg (Switzerland) The Lindenberg, peaking at 878 m, is a wooded hill in the Swiss Plateau north of the Alps, situated between the valleys of the Aabach, the Bünz and the Reuss. The hill draws a straight north-south line. On his ridge lies the border between the cantons of Lucerne (western slope) and Aargau (eastern slope and the northern half of the hill). Although the highest peak lies in the canton of Lucerne in the municipality of Müswangen, around 75% of the hill lies in the Aargau. The highest point is unspectacular as', 'title': 'Lindenberg (Switzerland)'}
