 {'idx': 10, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Franz Wognar Franz Wognar was an Austrian-Hungarian World War I flying ace credited with five aerial victories who held the rank of "Offiziersstellvertreter". Franz Wognar was born in Nagyszombat, Hungary, in the Austro-Hungarian Empire; due to subsequent changes in national boundaries, his birthplace is in present-day Slovakia. His birthdate was 6 January 1890. He was of Slovakian heritage. Wognar trained as a mechanic before enlisting in the Austro-Hungarian Army in 1913. He later transferred to aviation service during the first year of World War I. He was then trained as a pilot and sent into action when Italy entered the', 'title': 'Franz Wognar'}
