 {'idx': 17, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'minutes. Sonata for Two Violins (Prokofiev) Sergei Prokofiev composed his Sonata for Two Violins in C major, Op. 56, in 1932 during his vacation near St. Tropez as a commission piece to conclude the inaugural concert of Triton, a Paris-based society dedicated to presenting new chamber music. That concert was held on 16 December 1932. However, with the composer\'s permission, the sonata was performed for the first time three weeks earlier in Moscow, on 27 November 1932 by Dmitry Tsyganov and Vladimir Shirinsky, both members of the Beethoven Quartet. The performance at the Triton concert was the "Western premiere". The', 'title': 'Sonata for Two Violins (Prokofiev)'}
