[{'idx': 0, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Ornithopter An ornithopter (from Greek "ornithos" "bird" and "pteron" "wing") is an aircraft that flies by flapping its wings. Designers seek to imitate the flapping-wing flight of birds, bats, and insects. Though machines may differ in form, they are usually built on the same scale as these flying creatures. Manned ornithopters have also been built, and some have been successful. The machines are of two general types: those with engines, and those powered by the muscles of the pilot. Some early manned flight attempts may have been intended to achieve flapping-wing flight, though probably only a glide was actually achieved.', 'title': 'Ornithopter'}
