 {'idx': 4, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Esslingen (district) Esslingen is a "Landkreis" (district) in the centre of Baden-Württemberg, Germany. Neighboring districts are (from north clockwise) Rems-Murr, Göppingen, Reutlingen, Böblingen and the district-free city Stuttgart. Until 15 October 1964 the district\'s name was written officially as Landkreis Eßlingen. The district dates back to the Oberamt Esslingen, which was created when the previously free imperial city of Esslingen am Neckar became part of Württemberg in 1803. It was changed several times in the course of history. Since 1810 it belonged to the "Landvogtei Rothenberg" and from 1818 until it was dissolved in 1924 to the "Neckarkreis". In 1934', 'title': 'Esslingen (district)'}
