 {'idx': 7, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Shikoku is said to have been made by Genshin in the Heian Period. Genshin Genshin (源信; 942 – July 6, 1017), also known as Eshin Sozu, was the most influential of a number of Tendai scholars active during the tenth and eleventh centuries in Japan. He was not a wandering evangelist as Kūya was, but was an elite cleric who espoused a doctrine of devotion to Amida Buddha which taught that because Japan was thought to have entered "mappō", the "degenerate age" of the "latter law," the only hope for salvation lay in the reliance on the power of Amitabha.', 'title': 'Genshin'}
