 {'idx': 20, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Havriliak–Negami relaxation Havriliak–Negami relaxation is an empirical modification of the Debye relaxation model, accounting for the asymmetry and broadness of the dielectric dispersion curve. The model was first used to describe the dielectric relaxation of some polymers, by adding two exponential parameters to the Debye equation: where formula_2 is the permittivity at the high frequency limit, formula_3 where formula_4 is the static, low frequency permittivity, and formula_5 is the characteristic relaxation time of the medium. The exponents formula_6 and formula_7 describe the asymmetry and broadness of the corresponding spectra. Depending on application, the Fourier transform of the stretched exponential function', 'title': 'Havriliak–Negami relaxation'}
